QEMU 11.1.2: plain SEV (sev-guest, no SEV-ES) with an IGVM file fails with
"sev_launch_update_data: LAUNCH_UPDATE ret=-5 fw_error=2 'Guest state is invalid'":
the machine-done notifier takes LAUNCH_MEASURE (state launch-update -> launch-secret)
before the IGVM file is processed, which happens in the reset phase (backends/igvm-cfg.c,
igvm_reset_hold). Measured on the AMD EPYC 7443P host with Gramine's IGVM file and with
buildigvm's OVMF IGVM (Documentation/devel/sev/FINDINGS.md 2026-10-16, phase 1).

Fix: with an IGVM file, do not register the notifier; take the measurement when the VM
starts running, right before LAUNCH_FINISH (a no-op when it was taken already). The
measurement is then available through query-sev-launch-measure once the guest runs; a
guest owner that wants to inject a secret before the first instruction cannot use IGVM
with plain SEV this way. SEV-SNP is not affected.

--- a/target/i386/sev.c
+++ b/target/i386/sev.c
@@ -1663,6 +1663,14 @@
 
     if (running) {
         if (!sev_check_state(sev_common, SEV_STATE_RUNNING)) {
+            /*
+             * An IGVM file is loaded in the reset phase, after the machine-done
+             * notifier that measures the other SEV guests: measure here, after
+             * its LAUNCH_UPDATE_DATA calls (no-op if already measured).
+             */
+            if (!sev_snp_enabled()) {
+                sev_launch_get_measure(NULL, NULL);
+            }
             klass->launch_finish(sev_common);
 
             /* add migration blocker */
@@ -1973,7 +1981,9 @@
          * be collected without any reliance on the VMM. So skip registering
          * the notifier for SNP in favor of using guest attestation instead.
          */
-        qemu_add_machine_init_done_notifier(&sev_machine_done_notify);
+        if (!X86_MACHINE(qdev_get_machine())->igvm) {
+            qemu_add_machine_init_done_notifier(&sev_machine_done_notify);
+        }
     }
     return 0;
 }
